Subject: [PATCH 06864/11362] [outer-loop] ARC sp80 round-4: honest null, L6
 (final level) elbow-alignment finding

Round-4 codex gpt-5.6-sol attempt on sp80 tests L6 (the final level,
win_levels=6). New geometric finding: elbow routing depends on one-cell
alignment -- a downward stream aimed at an elbow's vertical stem can
double-leak (spill down its inner side as well as turn), while offsetting
the elbow so the stream meets its horizontal arm instead eliminates one
leakage path. An offset candidate filled all four visible sockets but
still leaked one stray stream, and a fresh-reset reproduce() gate on a
compressed 36-action candidate reached only level 5 -- confirming that
filling all visible sockets is insufficient while any stray stream
remains. Also reconfirms ACTION5 commits are a scarce per-episode resource
(5 commits ended this episode).

Honest null -- no registry count change, frontier stays at level 5.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
